    switch opts.mode {\n           case modeBytes: return headBytes(r, os.Stdout, opts.count)\n           default: return headLines(r, os.Stdout, opts.count)\n           }\n       }\n       ```\n\n   - `cmd/head/head_test.go` (existing, 128 lines, needs modification)\n     - Uses `testutils.BuildBinary` and `exec.LookPath(\"ghead\")`\n     - Has `discardStderr` normalizer for error tests\n     - Currently tests: line counting, byte counting, negative counts, suffixes, mutual exclusivity, stdin, invalid input\n     - No tests for multi-file headers, -q, -v\n     - All tests use stdin — no file-based tests yet\n     - Helper function `bytes512()` generates 600 bytes of test data\n\n   - `pkg/testutils/difftest.go` (from package_contracts)\n     - `DiffTest` struct has: Name, Args, Stdin, Env, WorkDir, ExitCode, Normalize, ExpectedFiles\n     - `RunDiffTests(t, goBinary, refBinary, tests)` runs side-by-side comparison\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet — only file reading was done before the summary was requested.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Identified that the existing implementation needs:\n     1. A new `headerMode` type (auto/always/never) added to `options` struct\n     2. Flag parsing for -q, --quiet, --silent, -v, --verbose in both short and long flag parsers\n     3. Header printing logic in `main()` based on file count and header mode\n     4. The header format is `==> FILENAME <==\\n` with a blank line before non-first headers\n     5. New differential test cases covering multi-file headers, -q suppression, -v verbose mode\n     6. Tests will need temp files (via WorkDir or setup) since multi-file tests need actual files on disk\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - First message: Massive task description with role, repository_files, project_context (vision, architecture, specifications, roadmap, analysis, requirement_states), execution_constitution, go_style_constitution, task details, shared_protocols, and package_contracts. The task is \"[st